==Old English==

===Etymology===
From an earlier form {{term|hlāfweard|lang=ang}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*hlaibawarduz}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*hlaibaz||bread}} ( > {{term|hlāf|lang=ang}}) + {{m|gem-pro|*warduz}} ( > {{term|weard|lang=ang}}). Equivalent to {{l|en|loaf}} + {{l|en|ward}}. See also {{l|en|lady}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhlɑːvord/|[ˈɬɑːvɔrd]|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=hlāford|m|hlāfordas}}

# [[lord]], master of servants
# male head of a household

